---
import Shell from '../../../../../../components/AeroEvidenceShell.astro';
import summary from '../../../../../../../public/demos/aero/cep-01/benchmark-summary.json';
import qualification from '../../../../../../../public/demos/aero/cep-01/qualification-v2/qualification-summary.json';

const base = '/demos/aero/cep-01/';
const qualificationBase = '/demos/aero/cep-01/qualification-v2/';
const promptTokenCounts = Object.values(summary.context_measurement.actual_prompt_tokens_reported);
const minPromptTokens = Math.min(...promptTokenCounts);
const maxPromptTokens = Math.max(...promptTokenCounts);
const trackRows = Object.entries(qualification.tracks);
---
<Shell title="Aero · CEP-01 context efficiency and routing" description="A local-only benchmark of compact context, capability-based model routing, and deterministic report verification." path="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/context-efficiency-cep01/">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">AERO / CONTEXT EFFICIENCY · CEP-01</p>
    <span class="status mixed">INFRASTRUCTURE PASS · MODEL QUALIFICATION OPEN</span>
    <h1>Give each model only the context its task needs.</h1>
    <p>Revision 1.5 qualifies the context and routing infrastructure across six separate tracks. The engineering stack remains the authority; model qualification is intentionally still open.</p>
    <p class="metric">42 full-vs-progressive comparisons · 7 retained evidence states · 0 solver runs</p>
    <div class="links">
      <a class="primary" href={qualificationBase + 'REPORT.md'}>Read the Revision 1.5 report</a>
      <a href={qualificationBase + 'qualification-summary.json'}>Inspect Revision 1.5 results</a>
      <a href={qualificationBase + 'artifact-manifest.json'}>Verify artifact checksums</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="boundary" aria-labelledby="boundary-heading">
    <h2 id="boundary-heading">What this result does—and does not—show</h2>
    <p><strong>Demonstrated:</strong> six independently scoped qualification contracts, compact prompt construction, typed evidence expansion, capability-based routing, and deterministic claim checks over retained pass/fail/unknown states.</p>
    <p><strong>Not demonstrated:</strong> engineering-reasoning competence, CFD/FEA correctness, model reliability, or readiness for consequential decisions. The run is a public metadata fixture and contains no physical simulation or provider calls.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="tracks-heading">
    <h2 id="tracks-heading">Six claims, six qualification tracks</h2>
    <div class="cards">
      {trackRows.map(([trackId, track]) => <article><h3><code>{trackId}</code> {track.name}</h3><p>{track.claim}</p><span class="status mixed">{track.status.replaceAll('_', ' ')}</span><p class="subtle">{track.cases.length} retained cases · model calls {track.model_calls} · solver runs {qualification.solver_runs}</p></article>)}
    </div>
    <p class="subtle">A track-level infrastructure pass is not a universal “model passed Aero” verdict. Provider qualification requires held-out, repeated runs for each track.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="context-heading">
    <h2 id="context-heading">Context measurement</h2>
    <p>The full-context comparator was constructed locally and never sent to a model. Across 42 fixture comparisons, the progressive view is an indicative {qualification.context_summary.mean_estimated_reduction_percent}% smaller (range {qualification.context_summary.min_estimated_reduction_percent}–{qualification.context_summary.max_estimated_reduction_percent}%). These are serialization estimates, not tokenizer-equivalent or cost guarantees.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <article><h3>Full-context comparator</h3><p class="metric">Synthetic measurement payload</p><p>Contains repeated history/log/metadata scaffolding; not transmitted.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Progressive context</h3><p class="metric">Decision summary first</p><p>Typed Level 2 evidence expands only when the track needs it.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="model-heading">
    <h2 id="model-heading">Historical local report-drafting sample</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Local profile</th><th>Disposition</th><th>Input tokens</th><th>Verifier findings</th><th>Latency</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      {summary.model_results.map((result) => <tr>
        <th>{result.model}</th>
        <td>{result.disposition.replaceAll('_', ' ')}</td>
        <td>{result.reported_prompt_tokens}</td>
        <td>{result.findings.length ? result.findings.map((item) => item.replaceAll('_', ' ')).join('; ') : 'None detected on this sample'}</td>
        <td>{result.latency_seconds.toFixed(2)} s</td>
      </tr>)}
    </tbody></table></div>
    <p class="subtle">This older one-fixture provider run remains linked for provenance. Its 72B result was a single-sample passer only; it cannot establish a reliable model ranking or qualification.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="architecture-heading">
    <h2 id="architecture-heading">Authority stays with evidence</h2>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li><strong>Classify</strong><span>Task, consequence, complexity, and context budget</span></li>
      <li><strong>Summarize</strong><span>Decision-grade facts and open gates by default</span></li>
      <li><strong>Expand</strong><span>Typed evidence retrieved only when requested</span></li>
      <li><strong>Route</strong><span>Choose by declared task capability, not a fixed model name</span></li>
      <li><strong>Verify</strong><span>Check generated prose against authoritative facts</span></li>
      <li><strong>Escalate</strong><span>Return uncertainty or high-consequence decisions for human review</span></li>
    </ol>
    <p>Deterministic software remains responsible for calculations, thresholds, hashes, gate states, and provenance. Models may explain or draft; they cannot promote numerical acceptability or design readiness.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="boundary" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
    <h2 id="next-heading">What remains</h2>
    <p>The next meaningful test is provider-backed, repeated, held-out evaluation for each track. Any changed disposition, lost unknown, or unsupported claim remains a qualification failure; the benchmark is not tuned away.</p>
    <p class="subtle">Revision 1.5 fixture date: {new Date(qualification.run_started_at_utc).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { timeZone: 'UTC', year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })} · Model calls: {qualification.tracks['CEP-R'].model_calls} · Physical solver executions: {qualification.solver_runs}</p>
  </section>
</Shell>
